            <ArticleTitle>[Doppler echocardiographic diagnosis of atherosclerotic aneurysm of the coronary artery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 74 year-old man with acute myocardial infarction submitted to thrombolytic therapy had the diagnosis of atherosclerotic aneurysm of the coronary artery attained with Doppler echocardiography. Subsequently diagnosis was confirmed by angiography and the atherosclerotic etiology identified in pathology.</AbstractText>
